  "body": "## What changed\n\nTwo user-reported issues on the just-shipped 5.5.0:\n\n### 1. Applying a restart-required websearch setting crashed the server\nSetting `WEBSEARCH_LOG_MAX_ROWS` / `WEBSEARCH_LOG_CONTENT_MAX_CHARS` from the Web Search page → instant server crash; the values applied after a manual restart. Root cause: `_run_supervised_server` fell through to `return ServerExitAction.STOP` when the runtime was still draining after `server.run()` returned, so a config-driven **RELOAD became a process exit**. The `serve()` loop is designed to re-run on RELOAD and the port-wait at the top of the next iteration handles the lingering socket, so returning RELOAD keeps the server up. **Reproduced** against a copy of the live `websearch.db` (server died after apply; the log showed a clean shutdown with no restart).\n\n### 2. Truncated websearch rows dumped raw JSON in the detail modal\nLegacy rows (stored before the 2M capture cap) render their `preview` — the first chunk of serialized output — as a raw JSON blob. `previewResultsFromJson` now parses the preview: it extracts the leading answer and walks the results array, pulling title/url/snippet from a result even when its huge `content` string is cut mid-way (the common exa shape). The modal renders readable answer + result cards; a note points to the raw pane for the exact stored preview.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Crash guard test** (`test_config_reload_not_degraded_to_stop_when_runtime_still_closing`): confirmed to **fail against pre-fix code** (`assert 1 == 2`) and pass with the fix.\n- **jsdom harness**: 28 assertions — input kv, full-output cards, collapsed raw JSON, truncated-preview parsing into readable cards, copy buttons, legacy-truncated notice.\n- **Live server** on a throwaway home (non-8082 port): `/admin/api/websearch/requests/1` (truncated row) renders answer + result card in the browser, not JSON. Live WSL :8082 untouched (health 200 at the end).\n- **96 tests** across the reload/static/websearch/analytics/export suites; full suite minus the pre-existing xdist-flaky entrypoint file is 3627 passed with the documented 16 PS-installer baseline; ruff/ty clean.\n\n## Versioning\n\nPATCH: **5.5.0 → 5.5.1**, `uv lock` regenerated in this commit.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The full `tests/cli/test_entrypoints.py` file is slow/flaky under this machine's xdist (pre-existing, unrelated to this change); the reload/replace/serve-supervisor tests pass individually.\n- Legacy truncated rows before the 2M cap remain truncated (unrecoverable); the new parser renders whatever the preview holds.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
