    "message": "fix(cli): config reload must not silently exit the process; parse truncated websearch previews into readable cards\n\nTwo user-reported issues on 5.5.0:\n\n1. Applying a restart-required setting (e.g. WEBSEARCH_LOG_MAX_ROWS /\n   WEBSEARCH_LOG_CONTENT_MAX_CHARS) from the Web Search page crashed the\n   server. _run_supervised_server fell through to return STOP when the\n   runtime was still draining after uvicorn returned, so a config-driven\n   RELOAD became a process exit. The serve() loop is designed to re-run on\n   RELOAD and the port-wait handles the lingering socket, so returning\n   RELOAD keeps the server up. Reproduced against a copy of the live\n   websearch.db (server died after apply); the guard test fails against the\n   pre-fix STOP and passes with RELOAD.\n\n2. Truncated websearch rows (all legacy rows stored before the 2M cap) dumped\n   the raw JSON preview into the detail modal — \"a ton of json data stuff.\"\n   previewResultsFromJson now parses the stored preview: it extracts the\n   leading answer and walks the results array, pulling title/url/snippet from\n   a result even when its content string is cut mid-way (the common exa shape\n   where content is huge page text). The modal renders readable answer + result\n   cards instead of the JSON blob; a note points to the raw pane for the exact\n   preview.\n\nVerified: reload guard fails pre-fix/passes post-fix; 28 jsdom assertions\n(input kv, full-output cards, collapsed raw JSON, truncated-preview parsing,\ncopy buttons); 96 tests across the reload/static/websearch/analytics/export\nsuites; full suite minus the xdist-flaky entrypoint file is 3627 passed with\nthe documented 16 PS-installer baseline; ruff/ty clean. Version 5.5.0 -> 5.5.1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
